WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.484
An app says it never sends your location.

00:00:03.484 --> 00:00:06.532
What does its network traffic actually show?

00:00:06.532 --> 00:00:11.322
PolicyTrace brings the promise and the evidence into one review workspace.

00:00:11.322 --> 00:00:14.370
Everything is processed locally in your browser.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:19.596
These demonstrations use synthetic data from a fictional app called Cedar Notes.

00:00:19.596 --> 00:00:21.371
First, the broken promise.

00:00:21.371 --> 00:00:27.584
The policy says it never sends precise location and does not collect device identifiers.

00:00:27.584 --> 00:00:29.359
Email collection is disclosed.

00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:35.128
Before running the check, I review the extracted claims and confirm their meaning.

00:00:35.128 --> 00:00:39.566
The result is two potential contradictions and one disclosure match.

00:00:39.566 --> 00:00:46.667
Opening the location finding shows the exact policy quote and the request containing a coordinate pair.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.442
Raw values are masked.

00:00:48.442 --> 00:00:55.099
The reviewer still checks whether these coordinates describe the user and whether the promise applies.

00:00:55.099 --> 00:00:56.906
Now the matching disclosure.

00:00:56.906 --> 00:01:00.521
This policy discloses all three observed data types.

00:01:00.521 --> 00:01:04.135
We get three matches, with evidence for each.

00:01:04.135 --> 00:01:10.461
That is a narrow data-type result, not proof of legal compliance or valid consent.

00:01:10.461 --> 00:01:13.615
The third case is just as important.

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:20.375
The policy denies sending location and collecting device identifiers, but the request body is missing.

00:01:20.375 --> 00:01:23.079
PolicyTrace reports insufficient evidence for both.

00:01:23.079 --> 00:01:28.037
It does not turn an incomplete capture into a passing result.

00:01:28.037 --> 00:01:30.415
Finally, I export a review.

00:01:30.415 --> 00:01:37.549
The report keeps source references while omitting raw identifiers, credentials, unknown hostnames, and free-form notes.

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:43.257
You can bring your own policy and HAR through the same workflow.

00:01:43.257 --> 00:01:50.867
PolicyTrace makes privacy review easier to inspect, easier to reproduce, and clear about what remains unknown.

